From 4fe047b1509ae37ba14b6474e425a0aaa1c56d7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 15:19:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: admin reload on tab switch + booking availability check
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two bug fixes:

1. ADMIN RELOAD BUG: Every admin view wrapped itself in <AdminLayout>,
   so switching tabs unmounted the entire shell (sidebar, theme,
   notifications, AdminCopilot) and remounted it fresh on every
   navigation. Fix: new persistent <AdminShell> holds all the chrome
   and stays mounted; <AdminLayout> is now a lightweight header
   registrar (same props, no admin view changed).

2. BOOKING AVAILABILITY BUG: Step 1 fetched ALL rooms and let users
   select any — including rooms already booked for their dates. The
   availability check only ran at final submit, so users filled in
   all guest details then got 'Room is not available' at the end.
   Fix: Step 1 now queries /api/rooms/availability and greys out
   booked rooms with a 'Booked' badge; booked rooms can't be selected.
   Also auto-clears selection if dates change and the room becomes
   unavailable, and sends users back to Step 1 if a race condition
   causes a submit failure.

Bonus: login API no longer 500s if the lastLoginAt audit write fails.

Files changed:
- src/components/admin/AdminShell.tsx (NEW - persistent shell)
- src/components/admin/AdminLayout.tsx (lightweight registrar)
- src/app/page.tsx (wrap admin views in AdminShell)
- src/app/api/auth/login/route.ts (resilient lastLoginAt update)
- src/components/public/RoomCard.tsx (booked state)
- src/components/public/booking/BookingFlow.tsx (availability in Step 1)
